 ('Operational weather', ['weather-runs','weather-history','weather-terms'], 'European coordinates; ECMWF original forecast runs from March 2024', 'Original forecasts, issue/availability times, explicit ERA5 replay reference', 'Reuse Open-Meteo adapter; commercial advanced APIs require appropriate plan. Free prototype access is non-commercial.', 'Shorter archive than climate history. No automatic stitched forecast or synthetic substitution.', 'A/B'),
 ('Solar cross-check', ['cams'], 'Historical record since 2004; European satellite coverage', 'Global, direct, diffuse and direct-normal radiation', 'Copernicus Atmosphere Data Store product access; qualify interval and licence metadata.', 'Shares atmospheric/satellite information with other products; disagreement is not independent validation.', 'B'),
 ('Land cover', ['clc'], 'European CLCplus Backbone 2023; 10 m raster', 'Cover classes, confidence/quality layers where supplied, usable-area masks', 'CLMS/WEkEO downloads and services; preserve CLMS attribution and edition.', 'Does not establish ownership, lease availability or permission to build.', 'A'),
 ('Terrain', ['dem'], 'Copernicus GLO-30; 30 m global surface model', 'Elevation, slope distribution and broad horizon', 'Copernicus Data Space / regional extracts; record product licence and attribution.', 'Vegetation and structures affect elevations; parcel levelling and near-object shadows need better evidence.', 'A'),
 ('Protected areas', ['natura','natura-service','england'], 'EU Natura 2000 plus separate national jurisdiction layers', 'Intersections, nearby designations, configurable avoidance distances', 'EEA spatial services/downloads; national open-data products under their own terms.', 'Selected screening policy is not a legal verdict. UK coverage is not supplied by an England-only layer.', 'A'),
 ('Parcel and planning', ['parcels'], 'Country/region-specific cadastral and planning data', 'Geometry, parcel IDs, zoning; uploaded lease and survey evidence', 'INSPIRE-compatible national services where available; rights/access evidence is obtained separately.', 'No uniform European database of available industrial land, asking price and development permission.', 'A/C'),
 ('Flood exposure', ['flood'], 'Europe and Mediterranean river basins >150 km²; return periods 10–500 years', 'Modelled flood-depth intersections and exposure flags', 'JRC/CEMS open downloads; CC BY 4.0. Higher-detail national layers as candidate-specific additions.', 'Not an official flood map; no automatic site failure probability or complete coastal/pluvial coverage.', 'A'),
 ('Water stress', ['wei','aqueduct'], 'European seasonal sub-units 2000–2023; global Aqueduct baseline/future indicators', 'Seasonality and regional water-pressure context', 'EEA downloadable data; WRI public datasets with attribution/registration terms.', 'Not a supply entitlement, delivered volume, treatment specification or usable rainfall model.', 'A'),
